<title>GERMANY: Adtranz wins 130 mln ecu rail contract.</title>
<headline>Adtranz wins 130 mln ecu rail contract.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rail systems company Adtranz said on Monday a joint venture in which it participates won a contract in Australia worth 130 million European currency units (ECU) to make electric railcars.</p>
<p>Adtranz said the deal was the largest passenger rail vehicle contract in Australia for nearly 10 years. The cars are to be designed by Adtranz but made in Australia by joint venture partner Evans Deakin Industries Ltd.  </p>
<p>The first vehicle is scheduled to be manufactured and delivered by April 1999 and the contract is to be completed by April 2001.</p>
<p>Adtranz is jointly owned by Swedish-Swiss engineering group Asea Brown Boveri and Daimler-Benz AG.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
